 scheme that will allow consumers  and businesses to sign up to a voluntary  scheme via their electricity suppliers  to be paid when they use electricity  away from peak time so that's charging  electric vehicles overnight charging  washing machines during the day avoiding  those Peak consumption periods during  the morning and evening because it is  warning that in a very worst case  scenario without that scheme in place  with a very cold period of weather with  issues importing electricity from from  Norway and others and potentially with a  gas shortage from European counter  counterparts and elsewhere there could  be periods of time when there are  planned blackouts for UK households  potentially for up to three hour blocks  at a time now this will be a real blow  for Liz truss who has been very  reluctant to talk about individual  Behavior change and reduction in  consumption and has promised there will  be no rationing well it's obvious that  the National Grid thinks differently and  campaigners are really saying look the  reason why even in this situation or  we're having to worry about this worst  case scenario is because we have failed  to invest adequately in the previous  decade or so in renewable energy in this  country in wind and solar power and in  energy efficiencies like home insulation  schemes and so on and had we done that  we wouldn't be reliant on fossil fuels  in the same way at all we will be  insulated from geopolitical events and  we wouldn't have to be thinking about  how to keep the lights on  well with the emphasis on the amount of  gas that will be available to fire power  stations let's take a look at our data  dashboard shall we and see just how much  of our energy Supply is being produced  by gas right now and you can see that  figure is 18.1 percent at the moment and  there's the figure for Renewables around  66 coming from Renewables at the moment  now as households across the UK worry  about affording their heating over this  winter Edinburgh council is to improve  the Energy Efficiency of more than a  thousand homes in the coming year after  receiving 5 million pounds of Scottish  Government funding the funding is to  specifically target areas of fuel  poverty and will provide wall insulation  to reduce heat loss from homes as well  as renewable Technologies such as solar  panels and battery storage  now the UN climate Summit cop 27 begins  one month from today in the Egyptian Red  Sea Resort of charmel Sheikh and at a  conference in the run-up to that Summit  the head of the Egyptian delegation has  attacked wealthy Nations for failing to  honor a climate Finance pledge  13 years ago at cop15 in Copenhagen the  Richer countries agreed to provide a  hundred billion dollars a year to  developing countries by 2020 and that's  a pledge that still hasn't been met  now a new study has found that the  drought that much of the northern  hemisphere suffered this summer was made  20 times more likely by climate change  that's already taken place now the study  concluded that a drought like this  Summers would have struck around once  every 400 years had the world not heated  up  but since human activity has increased  the global temperatures by around 1.2  degrees Celsius such a drought can now  be expected every 20 years  now the study also found that an  additional 24 000 people died across  Europe in part because of this Summer's  Heat  well let's get more on this from our  climate reporter Victoria Seabrook and  Victoria I guess the implication of this  is that we all have to expect more  droughts in the future now  yes exactly and that's really key is  just how widespread this was so we heard  that this is for the whole of the  northern hemisphere apart from the  tropical region where drought was 20  times more likely so we heard a lot  about drought in the UK two-thirds of EU  land was in drought at one point half of  the U.S big parts of China so this is  huge parts of the world all together 