f  disaster areas in the last couple months  last six months you know more uh more  fires have burned in the west and the  Southwest burned everything right to the  ground then in the entire state of New  Jersey the as much room as that takes up  and the reservoirs out west are are down  to almost zero we're in a situation  where the Colorado River looks more like  a stream there's a lot going on and I  think the one thing this has finally  ended is a discussion about whether or  not there's climate change we should do  something about it  well NBC correspondent Shaquille  Brewster was in Fort Myers when  President Biden visited  President Biden announced the opening of  additional disaster recovery centers in  this Fort Myers area and I've been at  one of them the first one to open just  yesterday here in Fort Myers talking to  people and it's really a fascinating  site that you see here we saw hours long  lines people waiting for more than an  hour to speak to a FEMA representative  many of them saying they didn't know  exactly what they were going to say or  what they needed from them but they  wanted some of those basic questions  answered questions like how did they  file a claim how long will that process  take maybe telling me one of the first  steps you need to do after a recovery  after you lost your business after you  lost the items in your home is file that  insurance claim if you have insurance so  this is a site where you also have many  private insurers here with their mobile  response units so if this is intended to  be a One-Stop shop for people in this  area talking with folks here as they  were waiting in line it was clear that  the need here in Fort Myers are really  in this entire area is so large one of  the questions that I asked them after  understanding their specific situation  is what would they want the the  president to know what would they want  the president to see on his trip I want  you to listen to some of those  conversations  uh just basically everybody needs help  and you know that it's not one person or  the other person it's everybody here  we're all uh you know Citizens United  States and you know you always see it on  TV all these places you know destroyed  and gone you always think those poor  people now all of a sudden it's US  President Biden's coming today do you  think he understands the tears that he's  seeing right now  well if he doesn't shed a fear or heal  himself I'd be surprised you know I mean  it's it's just unbelievable  and in this area there are signs of  progress we know that power has been  restored to the vast majority of people  the governor earlier today announcing  that Pine Island which has been closed  off since hurricane Ian made landfall  um that temporary Bridge has now been  built well ahead of schedule so you're  seeing signs of progress in this area  but when you're talking to folks and  when you're looking at the devastation  still so visible it is clear that  there's a long recovery ahead from so  many people back to you  well that's all for today thanks for  watching

